        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "647dcb81-1fc9-535e-97be-7eb7fc1fc21d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Camp Courtney, Okinawa, Camp Smedley D. Butler\n- People: Major Henry A. Courtney Jr.\n- Military Organizations: 3rd Marine Division, United States Marine Corps, United States Army, Imperial Japanese Army\n- Events: Battle of Okinawa, Operation Iceberg, Pacific War, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- On April 1, 1945, the Battle of Okinawa, codenamed Operation Iceberg, began with the invasion of Okinawa by United States Marine and Army forces against the Imperial Japanese Army.\n- The Battle of Okinawa included the largest amphibious assault of the Pacific War during World War II.\n- Major Henry A. Courtney Jr. was killed in action in the Battle of Okinawa.\n- Camp Courtney is named after Major Henry A. Courtney Jr.\n- The 3rd Marine Division is an infantry division of the United States Marine Corps.\n- The 3rd Marine Division is based at Camp Courtney, Marine Corps Base Camp Smedley D. Butler, and Okinawa, Japan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a24ccf66-fbae-56ce-b61c-06a47afc8bb4",
        "text": "Page: Camp Courtney. Sentence: It is named after Major Henry A. Courtney, Jr., who was killed in action in the Battle of Okinawa.\nPage: Battle of Okinawa. Sentence: The Battle of Okinawa (Japanese: 沖縄戦 , Hepburn: Okinawa-sen ) (Okinawan: 沖縄戦 , \"Uchinaa ikusa \" ), codenamed Operation Iceberg, was a major battle of the Pacific War fought on the island of Okinawa by United States Marine and Army forces against the Imperial Japanese Army and included the largest amphibious assault in the Pacific War during World War II, the April 1, 1945, invasion of Okinawa itself.\nPage: 3rd Marine Division (United States). Sentence: The 3rd Marine Division is an infantry division of the United States Marine Corps based at Camp Courtney, Marine Corps Base Camp Smedley D. Butler and Okinawa, Japan.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
